 "/description": [
  {
   "/narrative": [
    {
     "": "The development objective of the Resilient, Inclusive and Sustainable Enterprise Program for Results Project for Ukraine is to improve the enabling environment for a sustainable private sector-led recovery in Ukraine. The additional financing (AF) will co-finance eligible expenditures linked to disbursement-linked results (DLRs) expected to be achieved between January and December 2026 and will close the financing gap foreseen under the original design. The Program supports the implementation of selected components of the Government's National Economic Strategy (NES) 2021-2030 and the Ukraine Plan 2024-2027 across three results areas (RAs). These are: (i) improving efficiency of state support to small and medium enterprises (SMEs), with a focus on green competitiveness; (ii) improving the business environment and Government-to-Business (G2B) digital services; and (iii) enabling SMEs access to export markets.",
     "@xml:lang": "EN"
    }
   ],
   "@type": "1",
   "@xml:lang": "EN"
  },
